/*  Stashes — `Have <rabbit> bury <value>.`, `unbury`, a `For each` over a stash, and the refusals
    of the rewrite that turns a burying body into steps: the stash parts of
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.*.cs`, and the refusals of `src/Interpreter/StashTransform.cs`.

    ★ A function or method whose OWN body buries hands back a `stash of T`, where T is what it says
    it gives — the difference lives in its signature (`function-type-of`), so a call needs nothing new.

    ★ C# rewrites each burying body into a machine of steps once checking is over, and refuses what
    cannot be split: a `Return`, a bury inside a `Try`, a rabbit block, a task or a file block, a
    bury in a `for each` over something that is not a series, or in the `Otherwise` of a judgement
    whose leftovers cannot be named. Those refusals are asked here, after everything else, by
    walking each body the way the machine builder would; `stash-machine.cufe` then builds it.

    ⚠ A burying body's locals all land in one place, so a name may mean only one type in it, and no
    name in it may be a shadow.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    // ── Finding a bury ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The first node of one of `hits` kinds, not looking inside any of `opaque` kinds — or none.
    Bind node to stash-search, given (the node tree, the series of text hits, the series of text opaque):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "atom", return cast unknown-type.
        If kind is not "list":
            For each hit in hits, repeat:
                If kind is hit, return tree.
            Done.
            For each closed in opaque, repeat:
                If kind is closed, return cast unknown-type.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Define found as cast stash-search on (child, hits, opaque).
            If cast is-none on (found) is false, return found.
        Done.
        Return cast unknown-type.
    Done.

    /// `ContainsBury`: a nested function's bury is its own, so a `Bind` or a lambda is not looked into.
    Bind node to find-bury, given (the node tree):
        Return cast stash-search on (tree, a series with ("BuryStatement"), a series with ("BindStatement", "LambdaLiteral")).
    Done.

    Bind fact to contains-bury, given (the node tree):
        Return cast is-none on (cast find-bury on (tree)) is false.
    Done.

    Bind fact to contains-return, given (the node tree):
        Return cast is-none on (cast stash-search on (tree, a series with ("ReturnStatement"), a series with ("BindStatement", "LambdaLiteral"))) is false.
    Done.

    /// A `Stop` or `Skip` that would leave this statement for a loop around it.
    Bind fact to has-free-loop-exit, given (the node tree):
        Return cast is-none on (cast stash-search on (tree, a series with ("StopStatement", "SkipStatement"),
            a series with ("BindStatement", "LambdaLiteral", "WhileStatement", "RepeatUntilStatement", "ForEachStatement"))) is false.
    Done.

    /// What a function's signature hands back: a stash of what it buries, when its own body buries.
    Bind node to signature-return, given (the node statement):
        Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (returned) or cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) is false, return returned.
        Return cast wrapped on ("StashType", returned).
    Done.

    /// A function or method that buries has to say what it buries.
    Bind void or failure to check-buries-say-what, given (the node statement, the text what):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) is false, return.
        If cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) is false, return.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' buries values, so it has to say what kind", "",
            cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)), "declare '{name}' as void when it buries",
            "A burying {what}'s declared type is the type of what it buries: 'Bind number to {name}' hands back a stash of number.")).
    Done.

    // ── Burying and unburying ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Whether this type owns a region — a rabbit, or an object that says `and region`.
    Bind fact to owns-region unto checker, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is not "ObjectType", return false.
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1))).
        If definition is void, return false.
        Return cast conforms-as on (definition, "region").
    Done.

    /// `Have <agent> bury <value>.`
    Bind void or failure to check-bury unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        Cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define receiver as cast field-of on (statement, 4).
        If cast is-nothing on (receiver):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a bury has to name the rabbit doing it",
                "'rabbit' means the enclosing one, and a function body is not inside one",
                at-row, "bury with the bare 'rabbit' keyword inside a function",
                "Take a rabbit as a parameter and name it: 'given (the rabbit helper, ...)' then 'Have helper bury <value>.'")).
        Done.
        Define agent as cast unquoted on (receiver).
        Define found as cast one's look-up on (agent).
        Define owning as false.
        If found is not void, the owning becomes cast one's owns-region on (found's shape).
        If owning is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{agent}' does not own a region, so it cannot be told to bury",
                "Burying suspends the work in a region, so the thing told to do it has to own one",
                at-row, "have '{agent}' bury a value",
                "Take a rabbit as a parameter — 'given (the rabbit {agent}, ...)' — pull one with 'Pull a rabbit as {agent}.', or say 'and region' on the type '{agent}' has.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `unbury <stash>` — the next value, or void once the stash is spent.
    Bind node or failure to infer-unbury unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define inner as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If inner's kind is "StashType", return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast field-of on (inner, 1)).
        Define said-first as "'unbury' needs a stash, but this is {cast type-words on (inner)}".
        If cast is-none on (inner), the said-first becomes "'unbury' needs a stash, and the type of what it was given can't be determined".
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (said-first, "", at-row, "unbury something that is not a stash",
            "A stash comes from calling a function that buries: 'Define s as cast walk on (tree).'")).
    Done.

    /// A lambda may not bury — only a named body becomes a stash.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-burying-lambda, given (the node body):
        Define suspension as cast find-bury on (body).
        If cast is-none on (suspension), return.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a function with no name cannot hand a value out and pause", "",
            cast numeric on (cast field-of on (suspension, 2)), "use 'bury' inside a lambda",
            "Give the body a name. A 'Bind' whose body contains a 'bury' hands back a stash, and a stash is an ordinary value — pass it wherever the lambda was going.")).
    Done.

    // ── A burying body's locals ───────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The type a local of the burying body being checked has — one per name.
    Bind void or failure to record-stash-local unto checker, given (the text name, the node shape, the number at-row):
        If one's recording-stash is "", return.
        Define key as "{one's recording-stash}\t{name}".
        Define already as the entry for key in one's stash-locals.
        If already is not void:
            If cast same-type on (already, shape) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "'{name}' means a {cast type-words on (already)} in one part of '{one's recording-stash}' and a {cast type-words on (shape)} in another",
                    "A burying function keeps its locals in one place, so a name can only mean one type there",
                    at-row, "use '{name}' for two different types inside a burying function", "Rename one of them.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        In one's stash-locals, the entry for key becomes shape.
    Done.

    /// A shadow cannot survive a burying body's flattening.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-stash-shadow unto checker, given (the text name, the number at-row):
        If one's recording-stash is "", return.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{one's recording-stash}' buries, so it can't shadow '{name}'",
            "A burying function is rewritten into one flat block of state, and a shadowed name would land on top of the name it hides",
            at-row, "shadow '{name}' inside a burying function", "Give the inner one a different name.")).
    Done.

    // ── A `For each` over a stash ─────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `For each <name> in <stash>` stands for the drain: take one, stop once it is spent, else run
    /// the body — and the drain is what is checked (`StashDrainLoop`).
    Bind void or failure to check-stash-loop unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define name as "it".
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false, the name becomes cast unquoted on (named).
        Define line-atom as cast field-of on (statement, 4).
        Define column-atom as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
        Define shadows as cast one's look-up on (name) is not void.
        Define spot as "{line-atom's word}:{column-atom's word}".

        Define taken as cast made on ("UnburyExpression", a series with (cast field-of on (statement, 2), line-atom, column-atom)).
        Define take as cast made on ("DefineStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name), taken, cast flag on (false),
            cast flag on (shadows), line-atom, column-atom, cast nothing)).
        Define alive as cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (
            cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (name), line-atom, column-atom)),
            cast atom on ("NotEqual"),
            cast made on ("VoidLiteral", a series with (line-atom, column-atom)),
            line-atom, column-atom)).
        Define arms as cast listed.
        Cast arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (alive, cast field-of on (statement, 3)))).
        Define stopping as cast listed.
        Cast stopping's add on (cast shaped on ("StopStatement")).
        Define inner as cast listed.
        Cast inner's add on (take).
        Cast inner's add on (cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (arms, stopping))).
        Define drain as cast made on ("RepeatUntilStatement", a series with (inner,
            cast made on ("BooleanLiteral", a series with (cast flag on (false), line-atom, column-atom)))).
        // Kept, so the loop it stands for can be replaced by it once checking is over.
        In one's stash-drains, the entry for spot becomes drain.
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Cast one's check-statement on (drain) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
    Done.

    // ── What the machine builder refuses (`StashTransform`) ───────────────

    /// Every burying body in the program, walked the way `StashTransform.Rewrite` reaches them.
    Bind void or failure to check-stash-machines unto checker, given (the node statements):
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is "BindStatement":
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
                Define body as cast field-of on (statement, 4).
                If (the entry for name in one's templates) is void:
                    If cast contains-bury on (body):
                        Define key as name.
                        If cast is-nothing on (target) is false, the key becomes "{cast unquoted on (target)}'s {name}".
                        Cast one's check-stash-machine on (statement, key) or pass the failure off.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Cast one's check-stash-machines on (body) or pass the failure off.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            If kind is "PullStatement" or kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Cast one's check-stash-machines on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If kind is "ObjectDefinition" and the number of (cast field-of on (statement, 12))'s children is 0:
                Define owner as cast def-name on (statement).
                For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                    If cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (method, 4)):
                        Cast one's check-stash-machine on (method, "{owner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}") or pass the failure off.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Cast one's check-stash-machines on (cast field-of on (method, 4)) or pass the failure off.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// One burying body: no `Return`, then every statement that has to be split, splittable.
    Bind void or failure to check-stash-machine unto checker, given (the node burying, the text key):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (burying, 7)).
        If cast contains-return on (cast field-of on (burying, 4)):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{key}' buries, so it can't also return a value", "",
                at-row, "return from a burying function",
                "A burying function finishes by reaching its end, and whoever holds the stash sees void once it is spent. Take the 'Return' out.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (cast field-of on (burying, 4), false, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to emit-stash-statements unto checker, given (the node body, the fact in-loop, the text key,
            the number at-row):
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            Define splits as cast contains-bury on (statement) or kind is "StopStatement" or kind is "SkipStatement".
            If splits is false and in-loop, the splits becomes cast has-free-loop-exit on (statement).
            If splits, cast one's emit-stash-control on (statement, in-loop, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Where a refused statement is said to be: its own line, or the function's when it has none.
    Bind number to stash-where, given (the node statement, the number at-row):
        Define place as 0.
        Judge statement's kind, where it is:
            "PullRabbitStatement" or "LaunchTaskStatement" or "PullStatement" or "ForEachFromInputStatement", the place becomes 3.
            "TryStatement" or "JudgeStatement" or "ForEachStatement", the place becomes 4.
            "WithOpenStatement", the place becomes 5.
            "ObjectDefinition", the place becomes 9.
            Otherwise, return at-row.
        Done.
        Return cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, place)).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to emit-stash-control unto checker, given (the node statement, the fact in-loop, the text key,
            the number at-row):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "BuryStatement", return.
            "IfStatement":
                For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (cast field-of on (arm, 2), in-loop, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
                If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
                    Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (otherwise-body, in-loop, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
            Done.
            "JudgeStatement":
                Define arms as (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children.
                Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
                // The leftovers an `Otherwise` resumes into have to be named, so the subject has to
                // be a closed union — unless the arms match values, which narrow nothing.
                If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
                    Define valued as false.
                    If the number of arms is greater than 0, the valued becomes cast is-value-arm on (item 1 of arms).
                    If valued is false:
                        Define subject-type as the entry for "{key}\tit" in one's stash-locals.
                        Define closed as false.
                        If subject-type is not void:
                            If subject-type's kind is "UnionType", the closed becomes (cast field-of on (subject-type, 1))'s kind is "list".
                        Done.
                        If closed is false:
                            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                                "'{key}' buries inside the 'Otherwise' of a judgement on something that is not a closed union", "",
                                cast stash-where on (statement, at-row), "bury from inside that 'Otherwise'",
                                "The leftover cases have to be named to resume into them, and only a closed union lists what they are. Judge a closed union, or move the bury out of the judgement.")).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
                For each arm in arms, repeat:
                    Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (cast field-of on (arm, 2), in-loop, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
                    Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (otherwise-body, in-loop, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
            Done.
            "WhileStatement":
                Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), true, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "RepeatUntilStatement":
                Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), true, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "ForEachStatement":
                Define spot as "{(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}".
                If (the entry for spot in one's stash-drains) is void and (the entry for spot in one's series-loops) is void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{key}' buries inside a for-each over something that is not a series", "",
                        cast stash-where on (statement, at-row), "bury while looping over a map",
                        "Resuming a loop means counting back to where it was, and a map's entries have no position to count to. Loop over a series, or use a While.")).
                Done.
                Cast one's emit-stash-statements on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), true, key, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "StopStatement" or "SkipStatement":
                If in-loop, return.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{key}' has a 'Stop' or a 'Skip' with no loop to leave", "",
                    at-row, "stop or skip outside a loop", "Put it inside the loop it belongs to.")).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define kind-words as kind.
                If kind is "TryStatement", the kind-words becomes "Try block".
                If kind is "PullRabbitStatement", the kind-words becomes "rabbit block".
                If kind is "LaunchTaskStatement", the kind-words becomes "task".
                If kind is "WithOpenStatement", the kind-words becomes "file block".
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{key}' buries inside a {kind-words}, which can't be split into steps", "",
                    cast stash-where on (statement, at-row), "bury from inside a {kind-words}",
                    "A Try block, a rabbit block, a task and a file block each carry something — a handler, a region, a thread, an open file — that a resumption cannot restore. Move the bury out of it, or use an If, a While or a judgement.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
